  "instance_name": "developmental_disability_reduced_identity",
  "label": "Developmental Disability Reduced Identity Stereotype",
  "description": "The trope that people with developmental disabilities are perceived as lacking individuality or complexity, often portrayed as having names or identities that are repetitive, simplistic, or easily categorized (e.g., 'Bob'). This stereotype reduces their humanity and ignores their capacity for nuanced expression.",
